        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Schur, Rashida Jones, Charlie Brooker, Joe Wright, Peggy Lipton, Quincy Jones, Kidada Jones\n- Works: Nosedive, Stoney End\n- Roles: teleplay writers, series creator, showrunner, director, actress, producer, singer, writer, musician\n\nFacts:\n- In 1968, Peggy Lipton originally recorded the song \"Stoney End,\" and her recording reached number 121 on the U.S. Billboard Bubbling Under the Hot 100 chart.\n- Rashida Leah Jones was born on February 25, 1976.\n- Rashida Jones is an American actress, producer, singer, and writer.\n- Peggy Lipton was married to musician and producer Quincy Jones.\n- Peggy Lipton and Quincy Jones were the parents of two daughters, Rashida Jones and Kidada Jones, who both became actresses.\n- For the episode \"Nosedive,\" Michael Schur and Rashida Jones wrote the teleplay based on a story by series creator and showrunner Charlie Brooker.\n- Joe Wright directed the episode \"Nosedive.\"",
